Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fluid: a phase the vessel's own closure is driving to
 nothing leaves (form 4, ii)

Physics. A boiling liquid in a rigid vessel with no room for a bubble does not boil: its pressure rises and holds it
liquid. The vessel's own balance at its energy and volume says so by where it goes: from the TP answer's vapour it
drives the bubble down towards nothing. Whether it arrives within its 24 iterations is a matter of numbers; the
direction is the physics. A phase the closure grows, however small, stands.

What the code did. The D26 amendment refused a proposed phase only where the closure ended under the trace share (1e-9
of the moles). Cold seed 48's liquid-full LNG tank beside dry ice stalls with its vapour at 1e-9 to 3e-9 of the moles,
still falling (57 % of its stalled own splits ended just above the share): the fold kept it, the step seeded it, the
next pass folded it, the pass key cycled and the interval halved (form A: 3.82 M Newton iterations in seed 48 alone).
One step of that tank (157.3903 K, 1.381 MPa, the closure stopped at 2.8e-9 of the moles at a residual of 2.4e-6)
ended in a phase/device active-set cycle.

What it does now. A proposed phase that a vessel's closure, converged or not, leaves under VANISHING_SHARE (1e-6 of the
node's amount: what a closure that stops short at a residual near 1e-6 resolves) and smaller than its start gave it is
being driven to nothing (vanishing). It is refused for the solve like one under the trace share, and a seed that would
add a refused phase is not taken. The one-tank step now takes one pass and one own split. In the review's rule-off
world (seed 48 with every unconverged closure adding nothing) none of the 40 stalled closures that add a real liquid
to a gas tank is refused: each grows its liquid, from about 0.3 to 0.56 of the moles. The one legitimate case it can
refuse is the first bubble of a vessel crossing its bubble point while that bubble holds under 1e-6 of the moles
(about 17 cm3 of vapour per m3 of LNG at 1.4 MPa) and the closure approaches it from the TP answer's larger vapour:
refused for that solve, it stands once larger. A junction's own split is the engine's converged PH answer and keeps the
trace share alone. New gate: one step of that tank holds no vapour in one pass; with the trace share alone it cycles.

Owner decision (2026-10-16), form 4.

